  abstract={Colorectal cancer (CRC) is a substantial global healthcare problem because of its high prevalence and mortality. Classical methods of diagnosis, although efficient, tend to lead to late-stage diagnosis, especially in resource-scarce environments. Newly developed artificial intelligence (AI) technologies, in particular, deep learning models, have indicated a great potential in enhancing the accuracy and efficacy of CRC diagnosis from medical imaging data. This work investigates the performance of AI-based techniques on different imaging modalities and publicly accessible datasets. It emphasizes the contribution of histopathological and radiological image analysis towards improved early detection, classification, and segmentation of colorectal tumors. The review also emphasizes the comparative efficacy of deep learning architectures for CRC, opening up the door for more trustworthy computeraided diagnosis systems.},
